{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1476557-mortals-and-supernaturals-in-the-same-game","id":1476557,"title":"Mortals and supernaturals in the same game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-17T01:07:00-07:00","id":1476557,"title":"Mortals and supernaturals in the same game","content":"I am not talking about hunters or supernatural merit template humans i am talking regular humans in the same party as a supernatural creature<br /> <br /> Have you ever done it? <br /> Do you think it makes things too complicated or do you believe there is any way to make it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T04:24:37-07:00","id":1476567,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot by the type of game you are playing.<br /> Without combat powers humans are easy kill, but if the game is more focused on political intrigues for example, you can simply award humans more character points to spend on merits and other traits.<br /> Minor templates or a couple of supernatural merits, and the right equipment( supernatural or not), can really help human charachters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T10:47:22-07:00","id":1476670,"title":"","content":"I briefly ran a mage game where one PC was mortal, and wanted to Awaken mid chronicle - although they were a Hunter (cheiron). The game didn\u2019t last long for other reasons, but the party balance actually worked out okay. The most important thing, I think, is making sure the mortal can be an expert in some relevant area of the chronicle, without a supernatural PC stepping on their toes, and making sure the everyone gets enough spotlight - and enough of the type of experience they were aiming for.<br /> I did try to \u201cbalance the scales\u201d a bit by giving the mortal an extra heaping of EXP (somewhere around 50, iirc), which let them create a seasoned hunter &amp; black market surgeon, and really dominate their party niche. So I do recommend that as well.<br /> But part of that decision is what kind of experience the player is seeking by choosing a mortal. It could probably work out to not grant bonus exp, if they want to be someone way out of their depth, but can leverage social / political / technological / ethical competence, as a lot of fantasy media likes to do.<br /> <br /> DFRPG did a pretty good job, I think, of enabling groups of mixed supernaturals and mortals; and the Accelerated edition even has a half dozen mortal templates that really emphasized the unique advantages mundane humans could bring (primary allies, resources, and being underestimated).<br /> And bonus Exp is essentially the fix in that system, too: a pure mortal gets 2 extra refresh, either to spend on more stunts, or to boost rolls and make narrative declarations. I know of a lot of DF games where a pure mortal was totally viable and a lot of fun.<br /> After running that system for a while, I find the supernatural templates underdeveloped, especially compared to Chronicles, and it\u2019s way harder to predict things like difficulty. So I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d recommend it over a Chronicles game. And Refresh is a different enough mechanic from Exp that it can\u2019t be easily converted. But I think it still makes a good comparison point for how that kind of mixed party can work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-18-2022, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T14:00:28-07:00","id":1476686,"title":"","content":"I'd guess that generally the more socially/politically complex your game is, the easier it'll be to have mortals. Like, if you have a complex society where supernaturals can't simply use violence to settle matters, it opens up opportunities for mortals.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Mage could be really interesting to play as a sleepwalker, softly working mages to achieve your goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[